From 14cdae365ee3a28eeebd1cda6eea433f92d982f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:53:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(client): a phone shows the start page's board 28% sooner

Every upright phone decoded the phone's picture, 2152x3172 at 2x, about
three times the pixels it shows. A phone's cut (phone-tall: 1052x2092 at
2x, the same lens and composition, cropped; 32 KB of AVIF against 37)
now shows on the windows it covers, fade and all (360x740 to 430x932);
the rest keep the whole picture. All three pickers (the head's preload,
the early picture, LandingPicture) share picturePlacement, bundled into
the head with the lens. The picture shown stays while it still covers
the window, so a phone's browser bars coming and going never fetch the
other picture (landingLens.test.ts, StartScreen.test.tsx).

Evidence: --primary --base db54330, cold-load, 12 pairs, SP3 alone on
the bench's measurement commit (bench/loop/ab-20261018-0317-sp3.md;
scoreboard change 1015:SP3): Start page shows the board, phone 796 ms
-> 564 ms, called better (every pair 0.66-0.80). No primary row called
worse; the desktop board leaned slower (median pair x1.25, 9 of 12),
with no code path of its own changed but the head's script: see the
run record.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011SfWVyoMjkEfNUzxfLRC8S
